How scheduling works

Pod definition file:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: 
  name: my-app
  labels: 
    app: myapp
    type: frontend
spec: 
  containers: 
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx
  nodeName:

#every pod has a field nodeName, that is by default is not set, kubernetes adds it automatically
when nodeName is not set, then schdeduler based on some algorithm will assign the node to the nodeName field
(if nodeName is already set in definition file, then scheduler will not comes into picture, the pod will be created in that node)

the scheduler goes through all the pods and looks for nodeName that does not have this property set
those are the candidates for scheduling

it then identify the right node for the pod by running the scheduling algorithm, once identified it schedules the pod on the node, byt setting the node name property by creating a binding object

#scheduler just assigns the best node for the pod, by mentioning the node name in nodeName feild, it will not make it run on that node

