if there is no scheduler to monitor and scheduler pods onto node, what happen

No scheduler

the pods continues to be in a pending state
now you can manually assign pods to nodes yourself
without scheduler, easiest way to scheduler a pod on a node is to simply set the node name feild to name of pod in pod definition file while creating the pod

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: 
  name: my-app
  labels: 
    app: myapp
    type: frontend
spec: 
  containers: 
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx
    nodeName: node-1

the pod then assigned to that node
you can only specify the nodename at creation time, you cannot reassign the pod to diff node if it is already running on a node

