manual Pod scheduling in Kubernetes

However, what if there is no scheduler (like kube-scheduler), you need to schedule the pod manually using nodeName feild

but you have already created a pod and it is in pending state, due to non assignment of node
now how can you assign it

1) oneway is to delete the pod and recreate it using upated definition file with nodename

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: 
  name: my-app
  labels: 
    app: myapp
    type: frontend
spec: 
  containers: 
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx
    nodeName: node-1

run: kubectl replace --force -f definition.yaml

this will send a kill signal to system and depends on the type of kill signal it handles the deletion on of the pod

this will delete the exisitng pod and recreate it with updated configuration


2) second way is to manually bind the pod with node

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: 
  name: my-app
  labels: 
    app: myapp
    type: frontend
spec: 
  containers: 
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx

the nodeName: field at the bottom of the left window is completely empty.
When you create this Pod, it sits in the Kubernetes database in a Pending state because no worker node has been assigned to run it yet.

#Pod-bind-definition.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Binding
metadata:
  name: nginx
target:
  apiversion: v1
  kind: Node
  name: node02

Linking Pod to Node: Because you cannot directly edit the nodeName field of an already-created Pod, Kubernetes uses a special Binding object (shown in the top-right window).

you create a Pod-bind-definition.yaml file with
kind: Binding
The metadata.name: nginx matches the Pod's name,
while the target section points to the chosen server (kind: Node, name: node02).

Sending the Binding to the API Server (terminal)
You cannot apply a Binding file using standard kubectl apply commands. Instead,send an HTTP POST request directly to the Pod's /binding/ endpoint on the Kubernetes API server.

curl --header "Content-Type:application/json" --request POST --data '{"apiVersion":"v1", "kind": "Binding" ... }' http://$SERVER/api/v1/namespaces/default/pods/$PODNAME/binding/




